{"id":"a5","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":6,"of":16,"title":"Adjectives agree","titleHe":"שֵׁם תֹּאַר","goal":"Put an adjective after its noun and match it in gender, number and definiteness.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"An adjective comes after the noun it describes, not before, and it copies three things from it: gender, number, and whether it has the article."},{"type":"table","caption":"גָּדוֹל — big","head":["","singular","plural"],"rows":[["masculine","יֶלֶד גָּדוֹל","יְלָדִים גְּדוֹלִים"],["feminine","יַלְדָּה גְּדוֹלָה","יְלָדוֹת גְּדוֹלוֹת"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"If the noun takes the article, so does the adjective: הַיֶּלֶד הַגָּדוֹל, the big boy. Leave the second הַ off and you've written a whole sentence instead — הַיֶּלֶד גָּדוֹל means the boy is big."}],"vocab":[{"he":"גָּדוֹל","en":"big","translit":"gadol"},{"he":"קָטָן","en":"small","translit":"katan"},{"he":"טוֹב","en":"good","translit":"tov"},{"he":"רַע","en":"bad","translit":"ra"},{"he":"יָפֶה","en":"beautiful","translit":"yafe"},{"he":"חָדָשׁ","en":"new","translit":"chadash"},{"he":"יָשָׁן","en":"old (of things)","translit":"yashan"},{"he":"קָשֶׁה","en":"hard, difficult","translit":"kashe"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["does, makes","then","big","asks"],"correct":2,"prompt":"גָּדוֹל","translit":"gadol"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["strong","eats","small","ordinary, used to"],"correct":2,"prompt":"קָטָן","translit":"katan"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["good","apartment","lord, master, sir","weight"],"correct":0,"prompt":"טוֹב","translit":"tov"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["bad","animal","moreover","justice"],"correct":0,"prompt":"רַע","translit":"ra"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["aeroplane","surprised","beautiful","Shvat (Jan–Feb)"],"correct":2,"prompt":"יָפֶה","translit":"yafe"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["grey","new","belief, faith","hears"],"correct":1,"prompt":"חָדָשׁ","translit":"chadash"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["watch, clock","and he went","old (of things)","Shvat (Jan–Feb)"],"correct":2,"prompt":"יָשָׁן","translit":"yashan"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “new”?","options":["נִצָּן","חָדָשׁ","הֲכִי","מַרְגִּישׁ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “big”?","options":["מוּזָר","יְרֻקָּה","תִּקְרָה","גָּדוֹל"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["גָּדוֹל","big"],["קָטָן","small"],["טוֹב","good"],["רַע","bad"],["יָפֶה","beautiful"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"What does הַיַּלְדָּה קְטַנָּה mean?","options":["The girl is small","The small girl","A small girl","The girl and the small one"],"correct":0,"why":"The adjective has no article, so this is a sentence, not a phrase."},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["קָשֶׁה","רַע","קָטָן","יָשָׁן"],"correct":3,"say":"יָשָׁן","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “hard, difficult”?","options":["קָשֶׁה","חַג","עִיר","מַאֲמִין"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"“The big house” is —","options":["הַבַּיִת הַגָּדוֹל","הַבַּיִת גָּדוֹל","בַּיִת הַגָּדוֹל","הַגָּדוֹל הַבַּיִת"],"correct":0,"why":"Both words take the article. Without the second one, הַבַּיִת גָּדוֹל, you've said the house is big."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “beautiful”?","options":["כָּתֹם","יָפֶה","מְבַקֵּשׁ","בּוֹא"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “small” in Hebrew","answer":"קָטָן","hint":"katan"}]}